  "content": {
    "id": "p39-q43-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "43",
    "prompt": "How many terms of the series $\\frac12+\\frac14+\\frac18+\\ldots$ give a sum of $\\frac{1023}{1024}$?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "10 terms",
      "worked": "$a=\\frac12$, $r=\\frac12$, $S_n=\\frac{1023}{1024}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}S_n&=\\frac{a(1-r^n)}{1-r}\\\\\\frac{1023}{1024}&=\\frac{\\frac12\\left(1-\\left(\\frac12\\right)^n\\right)}{1-\\frac12}\\\\\\frac{1023}{1024}&=1-\\left(\\frac12\\right)^n\\\\\\left(\\frac12\\right)^n&=\\frac1{1024}\\\\\\left(\\frac12\\right)^n&=\\left(\\frac12\\right)^{10}\\\\n&=10\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, 10 terms are required.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
